---
layout: base.njk
title: null
---

{# The home page is the introduction. Everything on it comes from `profile` and
   `sections` in src/_data/site.json, so adding a link or a section never means
   editing this template. #}

<div class="wrap">

  <div class="profile">

    <aside class="profile-aside">
      <img class="portrait" src="{{ site.profile.portrait | url }}"
           alt="{{ site.profile.portraitAlt }}" width="600" height="600">
      <h1 class="profile-name">{{ site.profile.name }}</h1>
      <p class="profile-role">{{ site.profile.role }}</p>
      <p class="profile-location">{{ site.profile.location }}</p>

      <ul class="profile-links">
        {% for l in site.profile.links %}{% if l.url %}
        <li><a href="{{ l.url }}" rel="noopener">{{ l.text }}</a></li>
        {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </aside>

    <div class="profile-main">

      <section aria-labelledby="about-heading">
        <h2 id="about-heading">About</h2>
        <p>
          I played hockey and baseball for Karnataka, spent fifteen years managing
          software programmes, and now build education programmes at the
          <a href="https://takshashila.org.in/" rel="noopener">Takshashila Institution</a>,
          where I'm Head of Policy School and Associate Dean.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most of that work is curriculum architecture — deciding what a programme
          should teach, how it should be assessed, and how you know it worked. I
          co-teach two courses on sport and public policy: <em>Building a Sporting
          Nation</em> with Nandan Kamath, and <em>Transforming Women's Sport in
          India</em> with Aditi Mutatkar. I also teach project management to
          athletes, working professionals and undergraduates.
        </p>
        <p>
          I write op-eds on sport, animal welfare and eldercare, and record a
          monthly episode of <em>All Things Policy</em>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The move from sport into a working life runs through most of it. I've
          made that transition myself.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="work-heading">
        <h2 id="work-heading">What I work on</h2>
        <dl class="deflist">
          <dt>Curriculum &amp; assessment</dt>
          <dd>Learning outcomes, assessment design, graduation criteria, and the feedback cycles that improve them.</dd>

          <dt>Sport &amp; public policy</dt>
          <dd>Two annual courses, op-eds, and the athlete-transition question.</dd>

          <dt>Programme management</dt>
          <dd>Twenty years of it — banking delivery at 130 people, now education.</dd>

          <dt>Writing &amp; podcasting</dt>
          <dd>Op-eds in national newspapers, a monthly podcast, and a newsletter on project management.</dd>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="made-heading">
        <h2 id="made-heading">Selected work</h2>
        <ul class="worklist">
          <li>
            <a href="{{ '/sports/timeline/' | url }}">Sporting Timeline</a>
            <span class="worklist-note">An interactive timeline of sport, politics, policy and natural events, from c. 2600 BC.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="worklist-title">Building a Sporting Nation</span>
            <span class="worklist-note">Annual course, with Nandan Kamath. Since 2024.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="worklist-title">Transforming Women's Sport in India</span>
            <span class="worklist-note">Annual course, with Aditi Mutatkar. Since 2025.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="worklist-title">Project Management Simplified</span>
            <span class="worklist-note">Newsletter on project management and leadership for practitioners.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      {% if site.sections | length %}
      <section aria-labelledby="sections-heading">
        <h2 id="sections-heading">Sections of this site</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-2">
          {% for s in site.sections %}
          <a class="card card-link" href="{{ s.url | url }}">
            <h3>{{ s.title }}</h3>
            <p>{{ s.blurb }}</p>
            <span class="card-cta">Open {{ s.title | lower }} &rarr;</span>
          </a>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </section>
      {% endif %}

      <section aria-labelledby="before-heading">
        <h2 id="before-heading">Before this</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          Fifteen years in programme and delivery management at EVRY and Wipro,
          latterly running a 130-person offshore team under CMMI Level 5.
          PMP-certified. M.Eng from Concordia, Montreal. I introduced
          <em>Sphygmus</em>, an inter-collegiate sports festival, which is now in
          its 30th year.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
        <h2 id="contact-heading">Contact</h2>
        {# Written as separate parts rather than a mailto: so the address is not
           sitting in the HTML as a string a scraper can lift wholesale. #}
        <p>
          By email: <span class="email">{{ site.profile.emailUser }}<span class="email-at"> [at] </span>{{ site.profile.emailDomain }}</span>
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>
